      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I understand your concern, but I strongly advise against giving your child salt tablets to rehydrate or replenish electrolytes. While salt can help with sodium levels, using salt tablets is not a recommended solution for pediatric dehydration and can be toxic if taken in excess. In fact, the American Academy of Pediatrics recommends Pedialyte as the go-to rehydration solution specifically designed for children's needs. rushing to the ER may take too long, but seeking personalized medical attention is still the safest option to address your child's dehydration.",
